      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **What is Series ?**\n",
        "\n",
        ">**A pandas 1-Dimensional labeled array that can hold any data type think of it as a single column in a spreadsheet(1 dimensional)**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OHn9l-Fobqlj"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "data = [100,102,110]\n",
        "# If i want to convert this list into a series i will use the Series() constructor.\n",
        "series = pd.Series(data)\n",
        "print(series)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "alW6-KuJccXm",
        "outputId": "4bd97197-636b-4b02-ac7e-427f5f6ffba5"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "0    100\n",
            "1    102\n",
            "2    110\n",
            "dtype: int64\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### **In the above example we used Series() constructor to convert a list into a Series.**\n",
        " >**As you can see in the output on the left hand side there are index of the entered series.**\n",
        "\n",
        " >**Below is the data type of the element in the**\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**The default behaviour of the index is to start from 0,1,2,3,... and so on but we can change this using the keyword argument name index in the Series constructor.**\n",
        "\n",
        " **for example:**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GUcODP05dMio"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "new = [10,20,30]\n",
        "new_series = pd.Series(new,index=[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"])\n",
        "print(new_series)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "CLYIIRjombvj",
        "outputId": "d9fd160b-a97d-4bfb-d129-3d993e12e282"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "a    10\n",
            "b    20\n",
            "c    30\n",
            "dtype: int64\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "As you can see in the above output the index of the given series changes according to what you put in the index arguments.\n",
        "\n",
        ">**But make sure the length of the series and index should be same to avoid any error**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "k_vkH-7Am8_2"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **If you need to access a value in the series by using the label/index directly than use loc[\"index\"] property.**\n",
        "\n",
        ">you can access a specific element at any index using the loc property. for example:\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "You can print the element at a specific index like this :\n",
        "\n",
        "print(new_series.loc[\"x\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "This will print the element at the x index\n",
        "```\n",
        "```\n",
        "To change the value at a specific index we can also use loc[] property.\n",
        "\n",
        "for e.g. new_series.loc[\"x\"] = 001\n",
        "\n",
        "This will change the previous value with the new value at the mentioned index.\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "15uP-hp_n0uW"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### **To Locate an element using the integer position of the series we use iloc[pos] property.**\n",
        "\n",
        ">If i type print(new_series.iloc[0]) it will print the element at the position 0 in the series."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UKC8oWovqeZn"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "##**How to filter elements in series?**\n",
        "\n",
        "To filter an element in the series we will add the conditions inside the subscripts -> [ ] . For e.g.\n",
        "> **print(new_series[new_series>110])**\n",
        "\n",
        "If we add condition inside this subscript it filters the element in the series according to our condition\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "QFlflo2-rZ9Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **Here's a more complex example we will be using python dictionaries instead of list to create a series.**"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UH3QTcXcs5a-"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "calories ={\n",
        "    \"Pizza\":300,\n",
        "    \"Burger\":200,\n",
        "    \"Hotdog\":150,\n",
        "    \"Coke\" :50,\n",
        "}\n",
        "# Converting the dict into Series.\n",
        "cal_count =pd.Series(calories)\n",
        "# Printing the calorie count series\n",
        "print(cal_count)\n",
        "print(\"\\n\")\n",
        "# To access a specific element at any index we will use loc and other property:\n",
        "print(\"Both the method cal_count['Pizza'] and cal_count.loc['Pizza'] gives the same result\")\n",
        "print(cal_count[\"Pizza\"])\n",
        "print(cal_count.loc[\"Pizza\"])\n",
        "print(\"\\n\")\n",
        "# To access using the position i will use iloc()\n",
        "print(cal_count.iloc[0:2])\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "PHRhbIKBs47c",
        "outputId": "de9624fa-3f25-42a1-be95-832ca3c437d9"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Pizza     300\n",
            "Burger    200\n",
            "Hotdog    150\n",
            "Coke       50\n",
            "dtype: int64\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "Both the method cal_count['Pizza'] and cal_count.loc['Pizza'] gives the same result\n",
            "300\n",
            "300\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "Pizza     300\n",
            "Burger    200\n",
            "dtype: int64\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
