      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **What is a Data Frame (df)?**\n",
        "\n",
        "A DataFrame in Pandas is a 2-dimensional labeled data structure—think of it as an Excel spreadsheet or SQL table in Python. It’s built on top of NumPy arrays but adds powerful features like named columns and row indexing.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Vku98WqY3qLf"
      }
    },
