    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "### **How to access this tables**\n",
        "---\n",
        "> df.head() : Use to access each rows form the start.\n",
        "---\n",
        "> df.tail() : Use to access each rows from the bottom.\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.columns : Allows you to access the header/columns of the table\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.index : Allows you to access the index of the table with additional info like start,stop,step,etc.\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.index.tolist() :Allows you to specifically access only the index.\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.info() : Gives all the detail about the table like data type,rows,columns,memory usage,etc.\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.describe() : Shows all the information about the table according to columns like count,mean,std(standard deviation),min,max,etc.\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.nunique() : Shows the count of unique numbers in each column.\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df[\"Column name\"].unique() : Shows all the unique values in the specified column.\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.shape : Shows the shape of matrix e.g. 2 * 2 ,3 * 3, 3 * 4,etc.\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.at[\"Row_label\",\"Column_label\"] : Allows you to access a specific element using the labels in the table\n",
        "---\n",
        ">df.iat[row_pos,column_pos] : Allows you to acces a specific element using the row,column position in the table\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "nY9I2ceT9gBL"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **Accessing Specific Data (Indexing and Selection)**\n",
        "1. Column Selection:\n",
        "\n",
        "    ◦ Bracket Syntax (df['column name']): This is the most robust method and works regardless of spaces in the name.\n",
        "\n",
        "    ◦ Dot Syntax (df.column_name): Only works if the column name is a single word.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Selection by Label (.loc):\n",
        "\n",
        "    ◦ Used to filter rows and columns based on labels (names or custom index labels).\n",
        "\n",
        "    ◦ Syntax: df.loc[rows, columns].\n",
        "\n",
        "    ◦ Can be used to select ranges (slicing) and to modify specific values within the Data Frame.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Selection by Position (.iloc):\n",
        "\n",
        "    ◦ Used to filter rows and columns based only on integer index locations.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. Optimized Single-Value Access:\n",
        "\n",
        "    ◦ .at (label) and .iat (integer position) are slightly more optimized if you need to grab only one single value quickly."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ejBm9LZtVnX9"
      }
    },
