    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **Aggregation**\n",
        "\n",
        "### **We use aggregate function  to :**\n",
        "* Reduce a set of values into a single summary value like (mean,max,min,etc).\n",
        "* Used to summarize and analyze the data.\n",
        "* often used with the groupby() function.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **As there might be some columns which are alphabetical so we might get some errors which using aggregation functions.**\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ">As we can only get the mean, max , min of a numeric value only we use numeric_only = True to get the mean of the integer based columns only."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3hnYXcz9qw1B"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Here is the list of some aggregate functions :\n",
        "\n",
        ">**mean( ) : Used to calculate the mean of the specified columns.**\n",
        "\n",
        "> **sum( )  : Used to calculate the sum of the specified columns.**\n",
        "\n",
        "> **max( )  : Used to calculate the Max of the specified columns.**\n",
        "\n",
        "> **min( )  : Used to calculate the min of the specified columns.**\n",
        "\n",
        "> **count( ) : Used to count the number of values in a column.**\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**We do not need to use  numeric_only = True in count func but need to use in the rest of the functions**\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AWTyd9HWs4O4"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(orders.groupby([\"Type1\"]).mean(numeric_only=True))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "Y2Nki4vmq0zL",
