    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# **Data Cleaning :**\n",
        "* The process of fixing/removing incomplete, incorrect, or irrelevant data.\n",
        "\n",
        "* ~75% of work done by Pandas is Data Cleaning.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Drop irrelevant columns**\n",
        "\n",
        "> **orders = orders.drop(columns =[\"Legendary\",\"No\"])** : Removes the unwanted columns from the table.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Handle missing data**\n",
        "\n",
        "> **orders = orders.dropna(subset=[\"Type2])** : used to remove the row with na values at a specific column in it.\n",
        "\n",
        "> **orders = orders.fillna({\"Type2\":\"None\"})** : used to fill the na values with the specified value.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Fix inconsistent values**\n",
        "\n",
        "> **orders[\"Type1\"] = orders[\"Type1\"].replace({\"Grass\":\"GRASS\"})** : used to replace a specific value with the given value.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **Standardize Text**\n",
        "\n",
        "> **orders[\"Type1\"] = orders[\"Type1\"].str_lower()** : Lowercase the values in the specified column.\n",
        "\n",
        "5. **Fix Data Types**\n",
        "\n",
        ">**orders[\"Legendary\"] = orders[\"Legendary\"].astype(Bool)** : Converts 1 into True and 0 into False in the specified column.\n",
        "\n",
        "6. **Remove Duplicate Values**\n",
        "\n",
        "> order = **orders.drop_duplicates( )** : This removes the duplicate in the Table.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7lYvhZsXuxLG"
